Subject: [PATCH 9/9] FK-16 (0.3.32 candidate 5): verify both packages before
 promoting latest; lasting configuration refusals

From the independent review of 3debafa:
- publish-packages: before moving latest, both packages (also one published by an earlier, resumed run)
  must be served with the checked sha512; registry lag retried briefly; a mismatch stops with recovery
  instructions (latest unchanged, pending only).
- "No authority configured" and an authority credential that is not set are lasting refusals: an
  integration says "retrying will not change this", not "try again". Tested.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
